  "about": "How later meanings are built from older ones, in every UTP language. Each affix is a grammatical meaning the language gets as a root of its own (Vulcan's equivalents: ve 'person', -tor 'make', -hol abstract, -kam diminutive). A template turns a root of one part of speech into a new meaning, the way Latin, Japanese and most of the world's languages build their later vocabulary. A pack can switch templates off, limit them to fields, or move an affix in front.",
